    <string name="settings_fx_notice_title">About automatic exchange rates</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_source">Source: rates come from the public Frankfurter exchange rate service (api.frankfurter.dev), which compiles data from central banks and other public sources.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_when">When the app connects: it sends a request on the first launch each day, when the base currency changes, when this feature is turned on, and when you update manually. After a failed request it retries automatically at most once every 30 minutes.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_sent">What is sent: the base currency code, a fixed list of currencies and the requested dates. The service provider and network intermediaries such as Cloudflare can see your IP address and the time of the request.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_not_sent">What is not sent: balances, accounts, transactions or any other financial records.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_storage">Storage: retrieved rates are stored in the database on this device and included in backups.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_replace">When automatic exchange rates are turned on, the current rates are replaced with the retrieved values. If you turn the feature off, the most recently retrieved rates are kept; rates you entered manually cannot be restored.</string>
    <string name="settings_fx_notice_disclaimer">Exchange rate data is provided by a third party for reference only. It may differ from the rates actually offered by banks or other institutions and may be delayed or inaccurate. Valnook does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of this data, and neither the data nor any results calculated from it constitute investment, wealth-management or other financial advice.</string>
